@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex:      <http://example.org/sen0414-ch13ch14-lineage#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch13ch14-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Fresh narrow lineage: SEN0414 Chapters 13 and 14"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.5.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch13ch14-lineage/1.5.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch13ch14_lineage" ; owl:priorVersion <http://example.org/sen0414-ch13ch14-lineage/1.4.0> ;
    rdfs:comment "1.5.0 (2026-11-10): Owner approved both drafts (ST5_ApprovalGate -> Done). Render check (ST5_RenderCh13, ST5_RenderCh14): the approved drafts' content was found already present, correctly, in both chapters' existing deck and page (slide_text.py re-extraction of both decks matches the draft's six stories, slide outline and resources slide verbatim per chapter; both page HTML files' embedded slide prose carry the same six stories per chapter verbatim; cme_version_check_v1_0_0.py exit 0, 0 cross-file violations). No deck/page content differed from the approved draft, so no new version was declared for either chapter - same finding Lineage3 made for chapters 9-10 and Lineage4 made for chapters 11-12. Both set to Done on that finding." ;
    rdfs:comment "1.4.0 (2026-11-10): Both chapter drafts written for the owner's reading (DRAFT_ch13_v1_0_0.md, DRAFT_ch14_v1_0_0.md), consolidating the state-check findings - a write-up of already-correct content, not a correction pass, same situation as chapters 11-12. ST5_DraftCh13 and ST5_DraftCh14 moved to Done (drafted, not yet approved); ST5_ApprovalGate now Ready, blocking ST5_RenderCh13/ST5_RenderCh14 by the draft-first rule until the owner approves or corrects." ;
    rdfs:comment "1.3.0 (2026-11-10): Backlog stage. State check run for real: scripts/slide_text.py against both decks, both story-companion scripts re-run (sen0414_ch13_stories_v1_0_1.py, sen0414_ch14_stories_v1_0_0.py: 0 self-check failures, 6 stories each - story count not preset per the owner's 2026-11-09 principle, both chapters cover more distinct tools/concepts than chapters 9-12), both resources slides read, all 48 code examples checked (24/24 chapter-14 non-network examples re-run and matched exactly; 14/14 chapter-13 non-network examples re-run and matched exactly; the remaining 10 chapter-13 examples use requests/a weather API/Selenium/Playwright and cannot run in this sandbox - syntax-checked instead, 0 errors, and cross-read against the documented library calls). No gap found against the current standard in either chapter's story content, resources slide, or code - same clean finding as chapters 11-12. One legacy-duplicate finding, owner decided same turn: Chapter11WebScraping_YA_v1_0_0.pptx and Chapter12WorkingWithExcelSpreadheets_YA_v1_0_0.pptx (old-edition numbering) duplicated the current chapter 13 and 14 decks' subjects; owner approved retiring both now, same precedent as the four YA decks already retired for chapters 7-12. Both files removed from 03-materials/slides/ (recoverable from git history). Adds the draft, owner-approval-gate and (blocked) render stories for chapters 13 and 14." ;
    rdfs:comment "1.2.0 (2026-11-10): Objective stage - two objectives (owner-approved drafts: 0 to 2; chapter checks read and recorded: 0 to 2), each with its metric and baseline; mirrors Obj3_DraftsApproved/Obj3_StateChecksRecorded and Obj4_DraftsApproved/Obj4_StateChecksRecorded."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "1.1.0 (2026-11-10): Goal stage - two goals, one per scope deliverable (the draft, the checked-and-fixed materials), mirroring G3_DraftApproved/G3_StateChecked and G4_DraftApproved/G4_StateChecked. SELF-CORRECTION: v1.0.0's Mission-stage commit inadvertently also carried the Scope stage's content in the same file/commit, a lapse from the one-stage-per-commit discipline Lineage3 and Lineage4 both held to. Noted plainly here rather than rewritten - v1.0.0 stays as committed and pushed, append-only - and the one-stage-per-version pattern resumes from this version onward." ;
    rdfs:comment "1.0.0 (2026-11-10): Mission stage. Opened as its own narrow lineage, same pattern as Lineage3 (ch09ch10) and Lineage4 (ch11ch12), per the owner's standing rule to prefer simple, narrow, closeable lineages over one broad package-wide lineage, and confirmed again this turn ('plan chapters 13-14'). ORDINAL FINDING, checked against the live register before this was opened (lineage-practice-lessons.md: ordinals/IDs are taken from the live register's own next-free number, never assigned informally): the slides-lineage register (sen0414_slides_lineage_v2_402_0.ttl) already holds its own ex:Lineage3 (ordinal 3, exam work, LS_Abandoned) and ex:Lineage4 (ordinal 4, two-exams mission, LS_InProgress) - unrelated to, and in a different IRI namespace from, this session's ch09ch10 lineage (independently named Lineage3/ordinal 3 in its own file) and ch11ch12 lineage (independently named Lineage4/ordinal 4 in its own file). No technical/data collision (distinct IRIs), but the ordinal sequence was not actually unique package-wide as the convention intends; this happened because the two chapter-pair lineages were opened without checking the slides register's own ordinals first. Owner's ruling (asked, since it rests on no prior stated rule): note it here, leave ex:Lineage3 (ch09ch10) and ex:Lineage4 (ch11ch12) as the historical record unedited, and number forward from the true next-free ordinal across all lineage files found this turn, which is 5. This lineage therefore takes ordinal 5."@en .

## --- Profile declaration (ceremony step 1) ---

ex:ProfileDecl5 a backlog:ProfileDeclaration ;
    rdfs:label "Profile: AAL (agentic adaptive), default"@en ;
    backlog:declaresProfile backlog:Profile_AAL ; backlog:declaresLevel backlog:Level_L2 ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Default ;
    backlog:hasDeclarationRationale "Same declaration as Lineage3 and Lineage4 (ex:ProfileDecl, ex:ProfileDecl4): work is executed by an LLM agent, no human team; AAL is the default profile for agent-executed work and this lineage names none other. Level L2 stated plainly because this lineage does not re-run the full SHACL/register tooling used by the BRSF framework's own self-governance against this course repository's simplified lineage files." ;
    backlog:declaredAt "2026-11-10T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:reviewDate "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date .

## --- Lineage ---

ex:Lineage5 a backlog:Lineage ;
    rdfs:label "Chapters 13 and 14, narrow lineage"@en ;
    backlog:lineageForMission ex:Mission5 ; backlog:lineageOrdinal 5 ; backlog:lineageArchived false ;
    backlog:hasLineageStatus backlog:LS_Opened ;
    backlog:hasProfile backlog:Profile_AAL ; backlog:followsProfileDeclaration ex:ProfileDecl5 ;
    backlog:continuesFrom ex:Lineage2 ;
    rdfs:comment "ex:Lineage2 (sen0414-slides-lineage namespace) is the closed SEN0414 slides lineage this continues from, same as Lineage3 and Lineage4 before it. Chapters 13 and 14's structural retrofit (TK_Ret_Ch13_*, TK_Ret_Ch14_*) was recorded Done in that closed lineage before it closed, so no open item is carried forward; this lineage opens fresh on a mission the owner is stating now, parallel to, not continuing, Lineage3 or Lineage4."@en .

## --- Mission ---

ex:Mission5 a backlog:Mission ;
    rdfs:label "Chapters 13 and 14 taught from one approved draft each"@en ;
    backlog:missionFor ex:Backlog5 ;
    backlog:hasMissionStatement "Chapters 13 (Web Scraping) and 14 (Excel Spreadsheets) of the third edition are taught with a deck and an interactive page, each produced from one owner-approved chapter draft, following the same review given to chapters 9-10 and 11-12: a true, sourced, pedagogically-motivated story per concept the chapter actually teaches (per the owner's 2026-11-09 principle - story count is not preset, but important history of the concepts must be covered within time and scope), an accurate resources slide, and any open items named and closed before build." ;
    backlog:hasMissionOrigin "Owner's instruction this conversation, 2026-11-10 ('Fine proceed' confirming 'plan chapters 13-14'), following the Lineage3/Lineage4 pattern and their own stated exclusion that later chapter pairs get their own narrow lineages, rather than widening either mission." .

## --- Scope (taxonomic: areas, deliverables, exclusions - G194) ---

ex:Scope5 a backlog:ScopeStatement ;
    rdfs:label "Draft, check and (on approval) render chapters 13-14 only"@en ;
    backlog:scopeForMission ex:Mission5 ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_OwnerStated ; backlog:scopeCompletionState backlog:Proposed ;
    backlog:coversArea ex:Area5_StateCheck, ex:Area5_Draft, ex:Area5_Render ;
    backlog:hasScopeExclusion ex:Excl5_Ch1to12, ex:Excl5_OtherChapters, ex:Excl5_ExamWork, ex:Excl5_RenderBeforeApproval, ex:Excl5_StructuralRetrofit ;
    backlog:hasScopeDeliverable ex:Del5_ApprovedDraft, ex:Del5_CheckedMaterials ;
    backlog:hasScopeStatementText "IN: for chapters 13 (Web Scraping: HTTP/HTTPS, downloading files with the requests module, a weather API, parsing HTML, Beautiful Soup, browser automation with Selenium and with Playwright) and 14 (Excel Spreadsheets: reading and writing .xlsx files with openpyxl, setting font style, formulas, adjusting rows and columns, charts) of the 3rd edition only - (a) read the existing deck, page, research/ABox, the two chapters' already-self-checked story-companion scripts (sen0414_ch13_stories_v1_0_1.py, sen0414_ch14_stories_v1_0_0.py) and say plainly what is stale, missing, or duplicated against the owner's 2026-11-09 story principle and current resources-slide standard; (b) write one plain-text chapter draft per chapter (story per 5N1K using the real, already-sourced companion-script beats, explanations, slide outline, page-tab outline in slide order, each non-network code example with its executed result and each network/browser example checked for syntax and documented-library correctness, resources slide) for the owner's reading and approval; (c) ONLY after approval, render the deck, page and document from that one draft, versioned per the 2026-11-08 version rule (each file its own step, sized to the change). OUT: chapters 1-12 (chapters 1-8 midterm scope untouched; chapters 9-10 are Lineage3's own mission, 11-12 are Lineage4's own mission, neither widened here); chapters 15 and onward (later narrow lineages, same pattern); exam and mock-exam work (held outside this repository); rendering before the owner's approval of the draft; the structural chapter-check/retrofit against the iteration-20 standard (TK_Ret_Ch13_*, TK_Ret_Ch14_*), already Done in the closed Lineage2 and not reopened without a found defect." .

ex:Area5_StateCheck a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "What exists for chapters 13-14 today"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 .
ex:Area5_Draft a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "The one approved draft per chapter"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 .
ex:Area5_Render a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "Deck, page and document rendered from the approved draft"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 .

ex:Del5_ApprovedDraft a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Owner-approved plain-text draft, chapters 13 and 14"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area5_Draft .
ex:Del5_CheckedMaterials a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Chapter-13/14 materials checked against current standard, gaps named"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area5_StateCheck .

ex:Excl5_Ch1to12 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Chapters 1-12"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "Chapters 1-8 are midterm scope, untouched; chapters 9-10 are Lineage3's own live/closed mission and 11-12 are Lineage4's own closed mission, neither widened by this lineage." .
ex:Excl5_OtherChapters a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Chapters 15-25"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "Later chapter pairs get their own narrow lineages, same pattern as this one, Lineage3 and Lineage4." .
ex:Excl5_ExamWork a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Exam and mock-exam work"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "Held outside this repository." .
ex:Excl5_RenderBeforeApproval a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Rendering a deck/page/document before the draft is approved"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "Same draft-first rule applied in Lineage3 and Lineage4: layout built before content is settled was the measured cause of the five-build-per-page slowness." .
ex:Excl5_StructuralRetrofit a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "The iteration-20 structural chapter-check/retrofit for chapters 13-14"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "Already recorded Done in the closed Lineage2 (TK_Ret_Ch13_*, TK_Ret_Ch14_*). Reopening it without a found defect would be re-litigating a closed finding; this lineage's state-check (Area5_StateCheck) is the narrower, pedagogical-story-and-resources check only." .

## --- Goals ---

ex:G5_DraftApproved a backlog:Goal ;
    rdfs:label "Each chapter has one owner-approved draft"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope5 ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:Area5_Draft ;
    backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission5 ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Mission ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_OwnerStated ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ;
    backlog:hasGoalRationale "Direct reading of the mission statement: the draft, approved, is what the mission requires before rendering, same as G3_DraftApproved and G4_DraftApproved." .

ex:G5_StateChecked a backlog:Goal ;
    rdfs:label "What exists for chapters 13-14 is read and its gaps named before building"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope5 ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:Area5_StateCheck ;
    backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission5 ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Scope ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_OwnerStated ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ;
    backlog:hasGoalRationale "Same discipline as G3_StateChecked and G4_StateChecked: check what exists (deck, page, the already-self-checked story-companion scripts) against the owner's current teaching emphasis and standards and name the gaps before building, not starting from nothing." .

## --- Objectives ---

ex:Obj5_DraftsApproved a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Owner-approved drafts: from 0 to 2"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ;
    backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G5_DraftApproved ; backlog:fillsScope ex:Scope5 ; backlog:hasSuccessMetric ex:Met5_DraftsApproved ;
    backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ;
    backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "Count of chapter-13/14 plain-text drafts the owner has approved, read from his reply in this conversation." ;
    backlog:hasBaselineValue "0"^^xsd:decimal ; backlog:hasTargetValue "2"^^xsd:decimal ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase ;
    backlog:hasForecastDate "2026-11-12"^^xsd:date ; backlog:hasForecastRationale "Same two-day pacing as Obj3_DraftsApproved and Obj4_DraftsApproved: draft for the owner's reading, leaving time for checking and rendering before the week's lecture. A forecast at the pace delivered, not a deadline or promise." ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_OwnerStated ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .
ex:Met5_DraftsApproved a backlog:Metric ; rdfs:label "owner-approved chapter-13/14 drafts"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 .
ex:Obs0_Obj5_DraftsApproved a backlog:MetricObservation ; rdfs:label "Baseline, before any draft is read"@en ;
    backlog:observesMetric ex:Met5_DraftsApproved ; backlog:observationFor ex:Obj5_DraftsApproved ; backlog:hasObservedValue "0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    backlog:observedAt "2026-11-10T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:observedDuringCeremony true ;
    backlog:hasObservationMethod "No draft has been written yet; this stage only sets the objective and its baseline." .

ex:Obj5_StateChecksRecorded a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Chapter checks read and recorded: from 0 to 2"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ;
    backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G5_StateChecked ; backlog:fillsScope ex:Scope5 ; backlog:hasSuccessMetric ex:Met5_StateChecksRecorded ;
    backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ;
    backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "Count of chapters (of 13, 14) whose existing deck/page/story-companion-script state has been read against the owner's 2026-11-09 story principle and the current resources-slide standard, with gaps named in writing." ;
    backlog:hasBaselineValue "0"^^xsd:decimal ; backlog:hasTargetValue "2"^^xsd:decimal ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_OwnerStated ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .
ex:Met5_StateChecksRecorded a backlog:Metric ; rdfs:label "chapter-13/14 state checks recorded"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 .
ex:Obs0_Obj5_StateChecksRecorded a backlog:MetricObservation ; rdfs:label "Baseline, before either chapter is read this lineage"@en ;
    backlog:observesMetric ex:Met5_StateChecksRecorded ; backlog:observationFor ex:Obj5_StateChecksRecorded ; backlog:hasObservedValue "0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    backlog:observedAt "2026-11-10T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:observedDuringCeremony true ;
    backlog:hasObservationMethod "Not yet read under this lineage's own state-check story (ex:ST5_StateCheck, Backlog stage); the earlier facts gathered this conversation (iteration-20 retrofit Done, story-companion scripts self-checked 0 failures) are routing evidence for opening this lineage, not yet the state-check itself." .

ex:Obs1_Obj5_StateChecksRecorded a backlog:MetricObservation ; rdfs:label "Measured this turn: both chapters read"@en ;
    backlog:observesMetric ex:Met5_StateChecksRecorded ; backlog:observationFor ex:Obj5_StateChecksRecorded ; backlog:hasObservedValue "2"^^xsd:decimal ;
    backlog:observedAt "2026-11-10T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:observedDuringCeremony false ;
    backlog:hasObservationMethod "Ran scripts/slide_text.py against both decks, re-ran both story-companion scripts (0 self-check failures each, 6 stories each), re-ran all 24 chapter-14 code examples (24/24 matched) and the 14 non-network chapter-13 examples (14/14 matched; the remaining 10 syntax-checked only, 0 errors), and read both resources slides; findings recorded on ex:TK5_StateCheck_Ch13 and ex:TK5_StateCheck_Ch14 below, at target already." .

## --- Backlog ---

ex:Backlog5 a backlog:Backlog ; rdfs:label "Work admitted for chapters 13-14"@en ;
    backlog:hasIdentifier "Backlog_SEN0414_Ch13Ch14" ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ; backlog:isRegisterRoot true ;
    backlog:hasMember ex:ST5_StateCheck, ex:ST5_DraftCh13, ex:ST5_DraftCh14, ex:ST5_ApprovalGate, ex:ST5_RenderCh13, ex:ST5_RenderCh14, ex:ST5_YaRetirement .

ex:ST5_StateCheck a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "Read what exists for chapters 13-14 and name the gaps"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "ST5_StateCheck" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ; backlog:pursuesObjective ex:Obj5_StateChecksRecorded ; backlog:satisfiesDeliverable ex:Del5_CheckedMaterials ;
    backlog:decomposesInto ex:TK5_StateCheck_Ch13, ex:TK5_StateCheck_Ch14 ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done .
ex:TK5_StateCheck_Ch13 a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Chapter 13 state check"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK5_StateCheck_Ch13" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-11-10T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Deck SEN0414_Ch13_WebScraping_3e_v2_0_0.pptx carries all six real story slides from the self-checked companion script sen0414_ch13_stories_v1_0_1.py (Matthew Gray's 1993 crawler, the 30 June 1994 robots.txt courtesy convention, Leonard Richardson's 2004 Beautiful Soup, Jason Huggins/Paul Gross/Jie Tina Wang's 2004 Selenium, Kenneth Reitz's 13 February 2011 Requests, the Playwright team's 30 September 2020 Python preview), each matching its dated, named, sourced story text exactly. Resources slide (51/51) carries 15 live links matching the real sources (the book chapter, four tools' own documentation, two protocol texts, MDN, a video). 24 code examples checked: the 14 that need no network re-ran and matched the recorded expected output exactly; the 10 using requests, a weather API, Selenium or Playwright cannot run in this sandbox (no outbound network/browser) - syntax-checked instead (0 errors) and read against each library's documented call signatures. No gap found against the current standard. Legacy duplicate found: 03-materials/slides/Chapter11WebScraping_YA_v1_0_0.pptx (old-edition numbering, same subject as the current chapter 13 deck) - owner decided this turn to retire it, see ex:ST5_YaRetirement." .
ex:TK5_StateCheck_Ch14 a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Chapter 14 state check"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK5_StateCheck_Ch14" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-11-10T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Deck SEN0414_Ch14_ExcelSpreadsheets_3e_v2_0_0.pptx carries all six real story slides from the self-checked companion script sen0414_ch14_stories_v1_0_0.py (Dan Bricklin/Bob Frankston's 1979 VisiCalc idea pictured in spring 1978, Microsoft/Steve Jobs/Bill Gates's 2 May 1985 Excel-for-Macintosh announcement, the ECMA 376/.xlsx standard approved December 2006, Eric Gazoni/Charlie Clark's 2010 openpyxl, Thomas Herndon/Michael Ash/Robert Pollin's 2013 five-country Reinhart-Rogoff spreadsheet error, Mark Ziemann/Yotam Eren/Assam El-Osta's 2016 gene-symbol-to-date finding), each matching its dated, named, sourced story text exactly. Resources slide (51/51) carries 15 live links matching the real sources (the book chapter, openpyxl's documentation and tutorial pages, Python's own pprint/decimal/zipfile docs, the Library of Congress OOXML entry, Bricklin's own VisiCalc history page, the Genome Biology gene-name-error paper, openpyxl and defusedxml on PyPI). All 24 code examples re-ran and matched the recorded expected output exactly - no network dependency in this chapter. No gap found against the current standard. Legacy duplicate found: 03-materials/slides/Chapter12WorkingWithExcelSpreadheets_YA_v1_0_0.pptx (old-edition numbering, same subject as the current chapter 14 deck) - owner decided this turn to retire it, see ex:ST5_YaRetirement." .

ex:ST5_DraftCh13 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "Plain-text chapter draft, chapter 13"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "ST5_DraftCh13" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ; backlog:pursuesObjective ex:Obj5_DraftsApproved ; backlog:satisfiesDeliverable ex:Del5_ApprovedDraft ;
    backlog:dependsOn ex:TK5_StateCheck_Ch13 ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Written this turn: 03-materials/ch13/DRAFT_ch13_v1_0_0.md. A direct write-up of the already-correct six stories (Gray/1993, Koster/1994, Richardson/2004, Huggins-Gross-Wang/2004, Reitz/2011, Attam/2020), explanations, slide/page-tab outline (24 code examples: 14 re-run and matched exactly, 10 network/browser-dependent examples syntax-checked only), and resources slide - not a correction pass. Done means drafted, not yet owner-approved (that is ex:ST5_ApprovalGate)." .
ex:ST5_DraftCh14 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "Plain-text chapter draft, chapter 14"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "ST5_DraftCh14" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ; backlog:pursuesObjective ex:Obj5_DraftsApproved ; backlog:satisfiesDeliverable ex:Del5_ApprovedDraft ;
    backlog:dependsOn ex:TK5_StateCheck_Ch14 ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Written this turn: 03-materials/ch14/DRAFT_ch14_v1_0_0.md. A direct write-up of the already-correct six stories (Bricklin-Frankston/1978-79, Microsoft-Jobs-Gates/1985, Microsoft-TC45/2006, Gazoni-Clark/2010, Herndon-Ash-Pollin/2013, Ziemann-Eren-El-Osta/2016), explanations, slide/page-tab outline (all 24 code examples re-run and reproduced exactly), and resources slide - not a correction pass. Done means drafted, not yet owner-approved." .

ex:ST5_ApprovalGate a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "Owner reads and approves (or corrects) both drafts"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "ST5_ApprovalGate" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ; backlog:pursuesObjective ex:Obj5_DraftsApproved ;
    backlog:dependsOn ex:ST5_DraftCh13, ex:ST5_DraftCh14 ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Owner approved both drafts as written, no corrections requested, 2026-11-10." .

ex:ST5_RenderCh13 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "Render deck, page and document of chapter 13 from the approved draft"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "ST5_RenderCh13" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ; backlog:dependsOn ex:ST5_ApprovalGate ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Checked 2026-11-10: deck SEN0414_Ch13_WebScraping_3e_v2_0_0.pptx and page sen0414_ch13_page_v9_95_0.html already carry the approved draft's six stories, slide/page-tab outline, and resources links verbatim (slide_text.py re-extraction and page-prose grep compared against DRAFT_ch13_v1_0_0.md). No content delta found; no new version declared. TK_Ret_Ch13_* retrofit was already Done in Lineage2, unaffected." .
ex:ST5_RenderCh14 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "Render deck, page and document of chapter 14 from the approved draft"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "ST5_RenderCh14" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage5 ; backlog:dependsOn ex:ST5_ApprovalGate ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Checked 2026-11-10: deck SEN0414_Ch14_ExcelSpreadsheets_3e_v2_0_0.pptx and page sen0414_ch14_page_v9_97_0.html already carry the approved draft's six stories, slide/page-tab outline, and resources links verbatim. No content delta found; no new version declared. TK_Ret_Ch14_* retrofit was already Done in Lineage2, unaffected." .

